  "title": "Future Tense (Imperfective)",
  "titleRussian": "Будущее несовершенное",
  "description": "Compound future with буду + infinitive",
  "descriptionRussian": "Сложное будущее время с буду + инфинитив",
  "imageName": "arrow.right.circle",
  "intro": "The imperfective future describes actions that WILL BE ongoing, repeated, or in progress. It's formed with буду (conjugated) + imperfective infinitive. Use it for: processes (Я буду читать - I will be reading), repeated future actions (Я буду ходить каждый день - I will go every day), and general future activities without focus on completion.",
  "rules": [
    "Imperfective future always uses TWO words (буду + infinitive) — never just one word like perfective future.",
    "Use imperfective future for process, duration, or repetition: Я буду читать весь день. (I will be reading all day.)",
    "The question 'Что ты будешь делать?' (What will you be doing?) is one of the most common imperfective future phrases in daily Russian.",
    "Common mistake: using буду with a perfective verb. Never say 'буду прочитать' — perfective verbs form future by conjugation alone."
  ],
  "examples": [
    "Я буду читать книгу. (I will be reading a book.), ongoing process",
    "Мы будем ждать тебя. (We will wait for you.), duration",
    "Она будет работать каждый день. (She will work every day.), repeated",
    "Что вы будете делать вечером? (What will you be doing this evening?), process"
  ],
